  "_comment": "Fixture shared by the Go (internal/protocol) and TS (web/src/protocol) implementations; both must run it so they cannot drift. Contract: docs/30-protocol/websocket-protocol.md §9 (protocol version 2). seq is a string because it is a uint64 and values above 2^53 do not survive JSON.parse in JS. data_len is how many bytes the frame adds to seq: the payload length for OUTPUT / INPUT, 0 for SNAPSHOT (snapshot bytes do not count toward out_seq).",
